<title>CANADA: Manitoba pork packers go on strike.</title>
<headline>Manitoba pork packers go on strike.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 110 employees of the Jack Forgan Meat Ltd pork packing plant set up picket lines here on Wednesday morning after voting 81 percent to strike, a United Food and Commercial Workers statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;Our members have only had three raises in the past 10 years,&quot; UFCW Local 832 president Bernard Christophe said.</p>
<p>Jack Forgan officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>((Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
